{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The cry of the children of Israel has come to Me.</b> But did He not already mention above, ״ואת צעקתם שמעתי״ — 'and their cry I have heard'?" "<b>But</b> by way of the Kabbalah, ״צעקת בני ישראל״ — 'the cry of the children of Israel' — is Kneset Israel, which comes before Him crying out, in the language of (Genesis 18:21): ״הכצעקתה הבאה אלי״ — 'is this cry that has come to Me?'" "<b>And I have also seen the oppression.</b> Rabbenu Hananel, of blessed memory, explains: because they entered Egypt with seventy souls and Joseph settled them in the land of Goshen, yet the land could not contain them, for the blessing was upon them; and the Egyptians would not let them expand in the land, but rather they would press and crowd them. And he brings a proof for this from what Scripture says (Judges 1:34): ״וילחצו האמורי את בני דן ההרה כי לא נתנו לרדת לעמק״ — 'And the Amorites pressed the children of Dan into the hill country, for they did not allow them to come down into the valley.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:47.308270816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}